{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1523856-pet-semetary-bloodlines-requiem","id":1523856,"title":"Pet Semetary Bloodlines & Requiem","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-08T19:19:39-07:00","id":1523856,"title":"Pet Semetary Bloodlines & Requiem","content":"I'm currently watching Pet Semetary Bloodlines. It's not about vampires, of course, if you know anything about Pet Semetary you already know the general idea. But I was thinking this could be inspiration for either the birth of a bloodline or a new clan.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bPotential slight spoilers after this point:<br /> <br /> For those who haven't seen it Pet Semetary is a place of evil where anyone or anything that is buried there comes back to life. But they're not fully alive, they're undead monsters more like intelligent zombies than vampires and driven to kill in order to feed the evil place more death.<br /> <br /> I think if I were going to do them as a bloodline, I'd probably make them a Nosferatu Bloodline, with Nightmare, Protean, Resilience and Vigor. Their weakness would probably be tied to needing to feed on the recently dead or to giving up the first point of blood they drink from any given person to feed the evil. I might even make it unable to do a standard embrace.<br /> <br /> This is probably a better fit for Blue Book or Hunter but this was my first thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","user":"ShadowcatX","date":". 10-08-2023, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T20:02:30-07:00","id":1523857,"title":"","content":"Something of a swerve possibly, but if memory tricks me not, there's a Gangrel bloodline, the Oberlochs (from Bloodlines: the Hidden), with a devotion called Beloved Pet that does something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T23:17:07-07:00","id":1523862,"title":"","content":"I don't know about Pet Semetary, but that does look like a recipe for a 'bloodline' of Revenants.<br /> <br /> Or maybe a (preter)naturally occurring instance of zombie animals a la Raise the Familiar (Animalism 2), but 'unoccupied' by a vampiric master until fed Vitae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-09T06:43:07-07:00","id":1523874,"title":"","content":"I probably would write an intrinsically evil p-zombie sort of being like this not as a player-facing Requiem bloodline but as a horror or something unique like a Wicked Dead NPC-facing template.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}